sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243/0244 task, one Swamp run, Ansible phases for idempotent Node state (rule 22). docs/reference/node-provisioning.md.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: node:role:add
  %% kind: node.role_add
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane M icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>gets the role
  participant M as Metrics Node<br/>Prometheus
  CLI->>GW: node:role:add NODE ROLE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:role:add NODE ROLE`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> <role> [--converge] [--postgres-process=ID] [--clickhouse-process=ID] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node and the role, such as `app-dev`, `app-prod`, `ingress`, `database`, `websocket`, `analytics`, `ci-runner`, `gateway` or `swamp`
  %%> - `--converge` runs `node.role_converge` for a role the Node already has; it has its own chart
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, claim the role
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the target Node, and the target is an active, managed Linux Node
  %%> - the role is not `vpn` or `router`; those are protected from this command
  %%> - the Node doesn't have the role yet and holds no role it conflicts with; a singleton role such as `gateway`, `websocket`, `metrics`, `analytics` or `swamp` has no holder yet (`node:role:relocate` moves `gateway`, `websocket` and `metrics`; `swamp` cannot be moved)
  %%> - one add or converge Operation per Node (`operation.target_busy`)
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the role plan: packages, files, units, Caddy sites, PHP settings, firewall rules and certificate requests, and for `metrics` the Prometheus and Grafana specifications
  %%> Secrets:
  %%> - role credentials reach the run only through the vault, as key names
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the assignment is recorded as `provisioning`, and a task is recorded with the full intent
  %%> - a `provisioning` assignment with no Operation holding the Node for 11 minutes is a stale claim, left by an interrupted run
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-role-add
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task ID, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Require supported Ubuntu<br/>SSH argv · native assert
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Install Ansible<br/>native bootstrap
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the Swamp role provides the worker's Ansible; it installs the pinned version and collections first
  end
  SW->>N: Apply prerequisites<br/>Ansible phase: prerequisites
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the role's repositories and packages, at the pins of the release
  %%> - a Node of a task VM's nested fleet reads its apt packages through the VM's package cache (`apt_proxy` in the intent, else the archive)
  %%> Downloads:
  %%> - a pinned package comes from the mirror first; only a transport failure falls back to upstream, and a checksum failure stops the run and removes the staged file
  opt role needs Tool Managers
    SW->>N: Set up Tool Managers<br/>native child workflow
  end
  SW->>N: Apply the role<br/>Ansible phase: node
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the role's files, units, ports and storage directory owner and mode; protected paths are refused before any host work
  %%> On the swamp role:
  %%> - Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-07): a Swamp start cache that exists is given to the swamp account with mode `0644`
  %%> - the cache is the 10 MB file `/tmp/deno-compile-swamp.cache`; the swamp account can not replace a file of another owner in sticky `/tmp`
  %%> - an unreadable file makes every dispatch start about 0.35 s slower; no restart is needed to repair it
  opt Analytics
    SW->>N: Initialize Analytics<br/>native SSH argv · child
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - opens local storage, pulls the image, creates and migrates the database and applies the runtime
    SW->>N: Wait for Analytics<br/>Ansible phase: readiness
  end
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Install Swamp<br/>native steps
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - installs the binary beside the running one, links it, then applies the identity, the serve unit and the worker units
    SW->>N: Enable renewal<br/>systemd timer
    %%> Order:
    %%> - the Ansible node phase installs the renewal program and rendered units first
    %%> - start the timer after all three permanent workers are started; renew the oldest due worker only while its two peers accept dispatches
    %%> - active dispatches finish during each drain; two workers keep accepting work
    %%> - all three workers stay running; only one worker renews per round, after its two peers are accepting
    %%> - a failed or inactive worker can reset its failure limit and start while its two peers serve
    %%> Why not in place:
    %%> - replacing the running binary breaks every dispatch, so the running serve and workers keep working until they restart
  end
  opt role needs certificates
    SW->>GW: Sign role certificates<br/>native child workflow
    %%> Why this calls the Gateway:
    %%> - certificate signing is the one call a step makes to the Gateway
  end
  opt role changes PHP pools
    SW->>N: Publish PHP pools<br/>native delta publication
  end
  SW->>N: Publish role sites<br/>Ansible phase: publication
  SW->>N: Open the firewall<br/>Ansible phase: firewall
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - adds the role's rules, each specific allow before its isolation deny and the broader peer trust rule; unrelated rules stay
  opt role changes DNS
    SW->>N: Publish private DNS<br/>native delta publication
    %%> Why last:
    %%> - a name is reachable only after the site serves and the firewall is open
  end
  opt role joins Metrics
    SW->>N: Add the exporters<br/>Ansible phase: exporters
    SW->>M: Publish Prometheus<br/>Ansible phase: prometheus
  end
  SW->>N: Check the role<br/>Ansible phase: check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the one end check: the role's services, ports, sites and rules are in place
  %%> - on the swamp role it also checks that the swamp account owns and can read its start cache
  alt every step passes
    N-->>SW: role services ready
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the role active
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the assignment becomes `active`
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or no match
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Mark the role failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the assignment stays, marked `failed` at `converge:STEP`, so you can see it
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - finished host changes stay; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix the cause and run `node:role:add --converge`
  end
  opt run completed or failed
    SW->>SW: Remove the run folder<br/>private run files
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the intent, vault values and role configuration do not outlive the run, whatever its result
    SW->>N: Remove init containers<br/>best effort
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
